{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_02bf3680c86e6f29590633c15bd7cf3e2ab09589845a3b75f9599ca5c2312ae4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_621ae31c1d41fc920fa3371d1bba8321fd5b90a1e0b6daeaf2d9c7c5eef53e13"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"By design, the product omits several capabilities: bash dangerous-command blocking is only a regex blacklist (not a sandbox), retry is exponential backoff only (no fallback model or dollar budget), sub-agents are synchronous only, there is no RAG, and the MCP client implements no resources or prompts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0dbc28bf1e3bd2d2515e96271083a6becc65a96db72e04bc918953d55618d222","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0e3890f8757b8b6d96550ee756602bcfc9a04e82eacd220e84e226af67ed8d69","slc_59c166c2233de80fda2ea3afc08bb500f7a61633ebcc3aa799f348709f32a8e1"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"The product ships a CLI with an interactive REPL and a one-shot mode ('corecoder -p \"...\"' that exits when done), plus REPL slash commands such as /model, /compact, /tokens, /diff, /undo, /plan, /save, and /sessions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_118ad66701349223fd4d3c55e7ab88986120a50f572fe97d253e307e131ef864","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_df9b4a4e5718c814feea1142bf51172ec5730f33f9062ef6a905e8cffeb34cfd"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"The package layout includes agent.py (main loop, 213 lines), llm.py (streaming client, retry, cost, 267 lines), context.py (three-tier compaction), session.py, permissions.py, hooks.py, mcp.py, cli.py, config.py, and a tools/ directory with bash, edit, grep, glob, read, write, todo, and sub-agent tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_143e501554c75df257e6d5f7fb7f71a5686ac1e73a517369b02ea9093763ffcb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_14adac8dd0227a44d599e454085fc205c4e4fe5ecf962081cf78fdfba7ac5ddd","slc_2122ec6e560b444ff2b61c4adf407de07599e35988b24c84e513d45efcb5621d"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"If ~/.corecoder/mcp.json exists, MCP servers start as stdio subprocesses and their tools register as mcp__<server>__<tool>, treated like built-ins by hook matchers and the consent gate; the client implements only initialize, tools/list, and tools/call, with 15s handshake and 60s call timeouts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1525f581855ad425a957acebc0f6b4e1b386a2b20fcf223c174c3ff0a0a1745b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0e3890f8757b8b6d96550ee756602bcfc9a04e82eacd220e84e226af67ed8d69","slc_c82474a21d987d8835e1ca3ea977ff1aa31de5826486f01d8de740fb693eebeb"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"Sessions can be saved and listed under ~/.corecoder/sessions; session IDs are sanitized to safe filename characters so a malicious session name cannot traverse out of the directory.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_25353ac3b64ca924ddd111940ddcb15eb41c75a9c5558bc5f9ac4e83b253e624","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_90fc7a2884552fc6200666df94f3c110c4775e34c10814cd5e0f8bfc7e9e0b1c","slc_d3cfbe5011fa4d4b1f75df40a46d52cbf6d8cd344977388f89f0893c05734f9f"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"Hooks configured in ~/.corecoder/hooks.json run user shell commands around tool calls: pre hooks receive tool_name/tool_input on stdin and can veto with exit code 2 (stderr returned to the model), post hooks only observe, and hooks that error or exceed ten seconds are skipped with a warning.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2596d0ba20be1cd1ae724990abf96e64a718d61b59cff28eec02b938b27078d0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2853ebd8a9710800372c8f105fd7fa40449919fd5a1f3c39871ea32d2e7931f3","slc_4b86c6689fce72ab1dc96f7d7c4380492dcec75377e3d8569a84644539a30a36","slc_4bc7fa148d5826819fabfaa103358f9ceb1c6e988e2fead4192ff40a8c483345"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"The agent speaks the OpenAI-compatible API by default; providers are configured via environment variables (OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENAI_BASE_URL, CORECODER_MODEL), with an optional LiteLLM extra routing to a hundred-plus providers and .env loading at startup.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4bb5be2414b53f5f84636bfd8af20d00f735c9a812888b4eced17696053f9ef9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9c628ba761e95c02c7b82a010aa726df8e2c0f25b95e0072ccb5f4b3facb2ecb"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"Sub-agents get an isolated context and history with a toolset exactly one item shorter (lacking the agent tool, preventing recursive spawning), reuse the parent's model connection, truncate output past 5,000 characters, and run on a shorter round limit.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_67d12d7ab85fa33885beda9102dbb4fd24d797f13692586957683ae9ab8e1504","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4e1a2eb3cd1ded91328dc2796db768b20b25fd2744e50e307d0a702e44ca5b42","slc_be2cdddadcd2ea11599c431097fc35ff68a1b941c6e1411d9c78f9e01c9aacd7"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"CoreCoder is a Python 3.10+ coding-agent engine, MIT-licensed and published on PyPI as 'corecoder', described as a ~1,171-line engine within 2,398 total lines of pure Python.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9e7c4f8a1c92969547ddb06f9656e35e1e3979573fe0517fd072764f31ca9dcd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a812e8e43e8349255b4f2c860bb6bfb14ac91075b421065b0bff5969417172b9","slc_cab028894b431b14bb1753d48bf7f5af1dee9dd9b6053d9a27babe92c4c448ad"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"The package can be imported as a library: the top level exports Agent, LLM, and Config, and an example constructs an LLM with model, api_key, and base_url and calls Agent(llm=llm).chat(...).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_af02ca7869f469958835534f5ea616551575e61d3ba11059d328967af0976a16","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_17a7e1f5f5dd730fac71085fec55e3bb8a625ff392148405df321cfc1b0392fc"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"The agent loop is a bounded loop: it queries the model, runs requested tool calls in parallel, feeds results back, and returns when the model stops requesting tools, with a round limit preventing runaway execution.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b0a446043b2de82103f2b1847f4212b9cc2d8a1edbf1ae603b0d006585756db9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c17fe36589c2970f42a7a43b65684794da9aff07f2ce83929acfbe55838b7881","slc_fc56de2641daf92dc21b659c721c1166851253b65d954db3a052fdbeeedbfda7"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"Read-only tools (read_file, glob, grep, todo_write) run immediately, while mutating tools (edit_file, write_file, bash, sub-agent spawning) stop for user consent; the REPL offers allow-once, always-allow-per-tool, or deny, and one-shot mode refuses mutating calls unless --yes is passed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bb211f51f14236693c91a63d65896b07cd9aba11f68cd33cfaa4fda3ad0d866b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d939dba8bd45ac9e349524038d1bc35492bc6c7ff12aa285207784d0fe7f3905"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"Plan mode, toggled via /plan, refuses all mutating calls (writes, edits, bash, MCP tools, sub-agents) and returns refusals to the model as ordinary tool results until the user approves the presented plan; it is a single Agent flag plus a refusal branch ahead of the consent gate, with no plan file persisted.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f409b7a6cf74d358673d6cadfcecfa9ed67682fe9dcc31ec896434f3fe0bd2fd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c188f7cb66dd8f4df0f487f7cd87d3af6ed74d325f4309f1fd2a1ac1ca2361e0"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"edit_file uses unique-match search-and-replace rather than line numbers: no match returns the file start for re-anchoring, multiple matches require more context, and success returns a diff.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","created_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ffaf9029ce4641281d0c03dfa8831e498b21446dfd358b4c83f0ab03f8ff499d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"he-yufeng/corecoder@069948d180cb snapshot 3c89ac2ec67501ad","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2fb2c37644a2137fa314b9d13018988f6709d41b36310fb206d8e2b365a43f9c"],"source_ids":["src_d81855c1790553b290c6da2c923539bc"],"text":"Context is compacted in three tiers: at 50% full it trims over-long tool outputs mechanically, at 70% the model summarizes older turns while keeping recent ones verbatim, and at 90% it compresses everything to its tightest form.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:42Z","updated_by_operation":"op_870a8017155c4b83a732a3f4253d6312"}
